# =============================================================================
# SuperCool Finances — line-ending normalization (reproducible from zero).
# Default: normalize text to LF in the repo, check out native per platform.
# =============================================================================
* text=auto

# Files that MUST stay LF everywhere, or they break under bash / Docker / compose
# (a CRLF shell script fails with "$'\r': command not found" on a Windows clone).
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
# Datastore config / init scripts are bind-mounted into Linux containers, so a
# CRLF checkout on Windows must not leak in (e.g. a stray '\r' on a redis.conf
# value or a mongosh init script). Keep them LF everywhere.
*.conf  text eol=lf
infra/**/init/*.js text eol=lf

# Service source (NestJS, steps 3+). Kept LF everywhere: it is copied into the
# Linux images at `docker build`, and the lint gate (prettier, endOfLine=lf) runs
# it on every platform — a CRLF checkout on Windows must not fail lint or bake
# '\r' into a built image. Native-per-platform (the default above) does not hold
# for these.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Frontend source/docs (SPAs, spec 07). Same rationale as *.ts above: these are
# all covered by the prettier gate (endOfLine=lf), so a native CRLF checkout on
# Windows would fail lint/format:check. The backend is *.ts-only, so these
# extensions were absent when the rules above were written — pin them too.
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
